        "created_at": "2020-03-20T23:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'll make a note of your first point in the playtester thread, and I already called out the second.</p>\n<p>However, I'm not in agreement with the third.&nbsp; First, you should be creating environment twists in advance.&nbsp; On-the-fly twists are handled elsewhere in the book.&nbsp; Second, the color-coding makes it easy for me to spot zones easily enough, so the current format covers category, zone, and twist magnitude all at once.&nbsp; Putting zone as one of the axes would necessarily lose one of those.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
