        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I'll make a note of your first point in the playtester thread, and I already called out the second.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>However, I'm not in agreement with the third.&nbsp; First, you should be creating environment twists in advance.&nbsp; On-the-fly twists are handled elsewhere in the book.&nbsp; Second, the color-coding makes it easy for me to spot zones easily enough, so the current format covers category, zone, and twist magnitude all at once.&nbsp; Putting zone as one of the axes would necessarily lose one of those.</p>",
